<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-118-8.1-069> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The draft LS in R1-2407405 is endorsed with the following revision:
RAN1 has completed the work on RAN1 specification changes to support NR NTN for the frequency bands defined as part of FR2-NTN, and has endorsed several CRs to include FR2-NTN. During this work, RAN1 identified that some RAN1 specifications are still unclear regarding whether FR2-1 or FR2-2 procedure should apply to the FR2-NTN, as the current RAN1 specifications define different behaviour between FR2-1 and FR2-2. The attached CR R1-2407407 has been agreed.
Additionally, RAN1 has noticed that some RRC parameters (e.g., subcarrierSpacing in BWP) and UE capabilities (e.g., channelBWs-DL, configuredUL-GrantType1-v1650), which are expected to be applicable to NTN, may have the similar issues, i.e., only reference the FR1 and FR2-1 bands, or TDD-FR1 bands, TDD-FR2-1 bands and TDD-FR2-2 in the RAN2 specification. 
Furthermore, RAN1 understands that NOTE 2 in Table 5.1-1 of 38.101-5 states that FR2-NTN are regarded as FR2 bands, likely to minimize the impact when referencing RAN1 and RAN2 specifications. RAN1 would like to ask RAN4 to consider whether NOTE 2 may need to be updated. 

Final LS is approved  in R1-2407406.


Final summary in R1-2407404.


R1-2406163Draft CR on alignment on the indication of number of HARQ processes for PUSCHvivo
R1-2407294Summary of alignment on the indication of number of HARQ processesModerator (vivo)
""" .
