<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-118b-7-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The following TP is agreed for Rel-17.
------ Start of TP ------
If a UE is configured by higher layer parameter PDCCH-Config that contains two different values of coresetPoolIndex in ControlResourceSet, the UE may expect to receive multiple PDCCHs scheduling fully/partially/non-overlapped PDSCHs in time and frequency domain. The UE may expect the reception of full/partially-overlapped PDSCHs in time, only when PDCCHs that schedule two PDSCHs are associated to different ControlResourceSets having different values of coresetPoolIndex. For a CORESET without coresetPoolIndex, the UE may assume that the CORESET is assigned with coresetPoolIndex as 0.
------ End of TP ------
Final CR in:
