Endorse the TP below for TS37.213
----- Start of TP -----
4.5Sidelink channel access procedures
<Unchanged parts omitted>
For SL transmission(s) with multiple starting positions in a slot, the following are applicable:
-If a UE intends to transmit PSCCH/PSSCH in sidelink resource allocation mode 1 or mode 2 using a Type 1 SL channel access procedure, and if the UE cannot access the channel for the transmission from the 1st starting symbol of a slot, the UE shall attempt to transmit PSCCH/PSSCH from the 2nd starting symbol in the same slot according to Type 1 SL channel access procedure. There is no limit on the number of attempts the UE can make using Type 1 SL channel access procedure. 
-If a UE intends to transmit PSCCH/PSSCH in sidelink resource allocation mode 1 or mode 2 using a Type 2 SL channel access procedure, and if the UE cannot access the channel for the transmission from the 1st starting symbol of a slot, the UE shall attempt to transmit PSCCH/PSSCH from the 2nd starting symbol in the same slot and according to Type 2A SL channel access procedure.
----- End of TP -----
Comeback for the draft CR (Shohei)
