For CRC, adopt the TP below in Table 6.1.0.2-1 of Section 6.1.1.x.1 of TR 38.769:
***unchanged parts omitted***Table 6.1.0.2-1: CRC evaluationsCRC-6CRC-16TBSSourceCRC overheadPFA or PudSourceCRC overheadPFA or Pud8 bits[R1-9421-5][QUALCOMM119]43% ~10^(-8) Pud @10-3 BER[R1-9421-5][QUALCOMM119]67% ~10^(-11) Pud @10-3 BER12 bits[R1-9421-3][QUALCOMM119]33% 33%~10^(-2) PFA~10^(-8) Pud @10-3 BER[R1-9421-3][QUALCOMM119]57% 57%~10^(-5) PFA~10^(-11) Pud @10-3 BLER16 bits[R1-9421-5]27% [R1-9421-5]50% [R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]27%27%~10^(-7) Pud @10-3 BER[R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]50%50% ~10^(-10) Pud @10-3 BER24 bits[R1-9421-5]20% ~10^(-6) Pud @ 10% BLER and 2.7dB SNR[R1-9421-5]40% ~10^(-9) Pud @10% BLER and 2.8dB SNR[R1-9421-3][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]20% 20%20%~10^(-2) PFA~10^(-7) Pud @10-3 BER[R1-9421-3][QUALCOMM119]40% 40%~10^(-5) PFA~10^(-10) Pud @10-3 BLER32 bits[R1-9421-5][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]16% 16%16%~10^(-5) Pud @10-3 BLER[R1-9421-5][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]33% 33%33% ~10^(-10) Pud @10-3 BLER40 bits[R1-9421-5][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]13% 13%13%~10^(-5) PFA @10% BLER~10^(-4) Pud @10-3 BLER [R1-9421-5][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]29% 29%29%~10^(-10) Pud @10-3 BLER48 bits[R1-9421-3][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]11% 11%11%~10^(-2) PFA~10^(-5) PFA @10% BLER~10^(-4) Pud @10-3 BLER [R1-9421-3][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]25% 25%25%~10^(-5) PFA~10^(-10) Pud @10-3 BLER96 bits[R1-9421-5][R1-9421-3][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]6% 5% 6%6% ~10^(-2) PFA~10^(-4) Pud @10-3 BLER[R1-9421-5][R1-9421-3][R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]14% 14% 14%14%~10^(-5) PFA~10^(-9) Pud @10-3 BLER128 bits[R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]4% 4%~10^(-3) Pud @10-3 BLER[R1-9421-32][QUALCOMM119]11%11%~10^(-9) Pud @10-3 BLER256 bits[R1-9421-5][QUALCOMM119]2%2% ~10^(-3) Pud @10-3 BLER[R1-9421-5][QUALCOMM119]6%6% ~10^(-9) Pud @10-3 BLER***unchanged parts omitted***


R1-2410701Feature Lead Summary #2 for 9.4.2.1: “Ambient IoT – General aspects of physical layer design”Moderator (Huawei)
