<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-119-9.8.1-022> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement 
Further refine previous agreement  (made in RAN1#118bis)  on UE antenna radiation patternmodeling as follows:
For UE antenna radiation pattern modeling, consider the following options for further study:
Option 1) Adapt the Table 7.3-1: Radiation power pattern of a single antenna element
ParameterValuesAntenna element vertical radiation pattern (dB)AE,Vθ″=-min12θ″-90°θ3dB2,SLAV,θ3dB=FFS°,SLAV=FFS dBAntenna element horizontal radiation pattern (dB)AE,Hϕ″=-min12ϕ″ϕ3dB2,Am,ϕ3dB=FFS°,Am=FFS dBCombining method for 3D antenna element pattern (dB)FFSA″(θ″,ϕ″)=-min-AE,Vθ″+AE,Hϕ″,AmMaximum directional gain of an antenna element GE,maxFFS dBiNote: max direction gain and half power beam widths should be selected such that total antenna efficiency should be equal or less than 0dBi.

Option 2) half-wavelength dipole.
The normalized E-field radiation pattern of a half-wavelength dipole can be expressed as: E(θ) = cos(cos(θ)*π /2) / sin(θ), where θ is the angle relative to the +Z-axis
