<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-119-9.8.2-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement 
For near-field channel, for the non-direct paths, the distance d1 between the BS and the 1st point associated with cluster is generated with one of following options that to be selected in RAN1#120:
Option-1: The distance d1 is generated directly following a specific distribution.
For the k1 clusters, d1 = speed of light times the absolute delay of the cluster
For other k2 clusters, the distance  d1 is equal or less than the speed of light times the absolute delay of the cluster and generated following a specific distribution
FFS: The specific distribution, e.g., log-normal distribution for UMi
FFS: The values of k1 and k2
The generation of absolute delay of the cluster is according to the procedure defined in Section 7.6.9 in TR 38.901
FFS: The value for UMi, UMa, InH-Office.
Option-2: The distance d1 is generated by a scaling factor multiplied by the absolute distance corresponding to the absolute delay of the cluster, where the scaling factor is generated from a specific distribution.
For the k1 clusters, d1 = speed of light times the absolute delay of the cluster (i.e., the scaling factor is 1)
For other k2 clusters, the distance  d1 is equal or less than the speed of light times the absolute delay of the cluster and the scaling factor generated following a specific distribution (i.e., the scaling factor is equal or less than 1)
FFS: Distribution of scaling factor, e.g., Beta distribution for UMa
FFS: The values of k1 and k2
The generation of absolute delay of the cluster is according to the procedure defined in Section 7.6.9 in TR 38.901
FFS: The value for UMi, UMa, InH-Office.
Note 1: If d2 is agreed to be considered, the generation of d2 can follow the same principle with the generation of d1.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-119-9.8.2-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For near-field channel, in principle, one of following options is considered to calculate the antenna element-wise delay of direct path between TRP and UE:
Option-1: The following formula is used to calculate the antenna element-wise delay of direct path:
 τ1,u,s=τ1-d3D-|ru,s|c
where ru,s refers to the vector determined by the location of receive antenna element u and transmit antenna element s, d3D refers to the 3D distance between reference antenna at TRP and UE side.
The above formula is applied with the same principle as existing model in Clause 7.6.2 of TR 38.901, and the channel response of LOS ray between Rx antenna u and Tx antenna s at delay τ at time t is given by:
   Hu,s,1LOSt;τ=Frx,u,θθLOS,ZOA,u,s,ϕLOS,AOA,u,sFrx,u,ϕθLOS,ZOA,u,s,ϕLOS,AOA,u,sT100-1Ftx,s,θθLOS,ZOD,u,s,ϕLOS,AOD,u,sFtx,s,ϕθLOS,ZOD,u,s,ϕLOS,AOD,u,s 
exp-j2πd3Dλfexp-j2πru,s-d3Dλfexpj2πrrx,LOST∙vλ0tδτ-τ1,u,s
Option-2: The antenna element-wise delay of direct path is directly modeled based on the distance of direct path between antenna elements at TRP and UE side. 
Following formula is adopted to model the antenna element-wise delay in the channel coefficient as:
δτ-τ1,u,s,  τ1,u,s=τ1-d3D-|ru,s|c
where ru,s refers to the vector determined by the location of receive antenna element u and transmit antenna element s, d3D refers to the 3D distance between reference antenna at TRP and UE side.
Option-3: Confirm the following working assumption made in RAN1#118BIS:
“The existing model in Clause 7.6.2 of TR 38.901 is used to model the delay.”
Note: τ1 is same as that is defined in 7.5-30 in TR38.901


Final summary in R1-2410881.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-119-9.9.1-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
