R1-2500830Discussion on two candidate starting symbols for sidelink unlicensedSamsung
R1-2501438FLS#1 on 2 candidate starting symbols in TS 38.213Moderator (ZTE)
From Monday session
Conclusion (For Issue 1 in R1-2501438)
The specifications are aligned with the following, and no CR is necessary:
sl-StartSymbol is only used for operation without shared spectrum channel access.
sl-StartingSymbolFirst and/or sl-StartingSymbolSecond are only used for operation with shared spectrum channel access.
Conclusion (For Issue 2 in R1-2501438)
sl-StartingSymbolFirst will always be provided for operation with shared spectrum channel access, either as a default value or explicitly (pre)configured.


