From Friday session""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The guard period between the end of the downlink subframes and the beginning of the uplink subframes is fixed in specifications to be [48…50] ms at the ULSRP.
NOTE: This corresponds to the largest separation between DL and UL Iridium slot pairs. Adjustments to align with different UL/DL pair can be achieved by adjusting the common TA.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-002> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The downlink subframes within D=8 are fixed to: 
Option 1: [3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0] (across two consecutive radio frames).
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
NPSS/NSSS/NPBCH transmissions are dropped in non-D NB-IoT subframes 
NOTE: “non-D NB-IoT subframes” are subframes not contained within the set of D=8 usable consecutive downlink subframes in the TDD structure.
FFS: handling for SIB1-NB.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-004> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The non-U NB-IoT subframes are not considered by the UE as “NB-IoT UL subframes” from the specifications
NPUSCH is mapped as per current specifications.
NOTE: “non-U NB-IoT subframes” are subframes not contained within the set of U=8 usable consecutive uplink subframes in the TDD structure.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-005> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The non-D NB-IoT subframes are not considered by the UE as “NB-IoT DL subframes” from the specifications
NPDCCH / NPDSCH (not containing SI) are mapped as per current specifications.
FFS: additional NB-IoT TDD-specific rules for handling non “NB-IoT DL subframes”
FFS: Introduction of new periodicities for NPDCCH monitoring (e.g. by the introduction of scaling factor)
FFS: whether all the configuration values for NPDCCH are valid for NB-IoT NTN TDD.
FFS: handling of DL transmission gap
NOTE: “non-D NB-IoT subframes” are subframes not contained within the set of D=8 usable consecutive downlink subframes in the TDD structure.


R1-2501367Feature lead summary #2 on IoT-NTN TDD modeModerator (Qualcomm Incorporated)
From Thursday session""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For NPRACH, further consider the two options until RAN1#120bis:
Option 1: New NPRACH periodicities (multiple of 90ms) are introduced for NB-IoT NTN TDD.
Option 2: NPRACH transmissions are postponed in non-U NB-IoT subframes until the next U NB-IoT subframe(s)
FFS: The unit of postponement (e.g. PRU)
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
NPRACH format 2 is not supported in NB-IoT NTN TDD.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.11.5-008> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For segmented pre-compensation, RAN1 to further discuss at least the following options:
Option 1: Dropped/postponed NPUSCH / NPRACH are counted for segment determination
Option 2: A new pre-compensation segment is started at the beginning of each uplink burst
Option 3: UL segment should only be defined in consecutive U subframes
Option 4: Segmented pre-compensation does not apply for NB-IoT NTN TDD.
FFS: How to handle the UL segment gap.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.12-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
