<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.8.1-010> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For cases when a candidate antenna placement location is used for one antenna field pattern (i.e., not used for two distinct antenna polarization field patterns):
Reference radiation pattern of the UE antenna model is vertically polarized with all the gain in the theta filed component,
Fθ″″θ″,ϕ″=A″θ″,ϕ″ and Fϕ″″θ″,ϕ″=0.
For cases when a candidate antenna placement location is used for two distinct antenna polarization field pattern:
Reference radiation pattern of the UE antenna model is FFS,
For first antenna field pattern: Fθ″″θ″,ϕ″=FFS and Fϕ″″θ″,ϕ″=FFS.
For second antenna field pattern: Fθ″″θ″,ϕ″=FFS and Fϕ″″θ″,ϕ″=FFS.
Each polarized field component of the reference radiation pattern Fθ″″θ″,ϕ″ and Fϕ″″θ″,ϕ″ should be rotated according to the orientation of the each of UE antennae to get Frx,u,θ''(θ',ϕ'), Frx,u, ϕ''(θ',ϕ') and based on the orientation of the UE in the global coordinate system to get Frx,u,θ(θ,ϕ) and Frx,u,ϕ(θ,ϕ) using the methods already specified in TR 38.901, equation (7.3-3)/(7.1-11).


R1-2501430Summary #3 of discussions for Rel-19 7-24 GHz Channel Modeling ValidationModerator (Intel Corporation)
From Thursday""" .
