<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.8.2-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For near-field channel, for the non-direct paths, the distance d1 between the TRP and the 1st point associated with cluster is generated by Option-2:
The distance d1 is generated by a scaling factor (sTRP,n) multiplied by the absolute distance corresponding to the absolute delay of cluster, where the scaling factor (sTRP,n) is generated by:
For UMa scenarios, a Beta distribution with [α=1.8,β=1.22]:
For UMi scenarios, a Beta distribution with [α=2.35,β=1.45]:
For Indoor Office scenarios, a Beta distribution with [α=1.13,β=1.42]
For the value of  k1 and  k2
For UMa, the value of  k1 is 2.
For UMi, the value of  k1 is 2.
For InH, the value  k1 is [75%, 10.9%] of the total number of clusters for InH
Note: the  k1 clusters are the strongest of the total number of clusters in the channel
Note: the value of  k2 is equal to total number of clusters minus k1.


R1-2501484Summary#3 of channel model adaptation and extensionModerator (ZTE)
From Thursday session""" .
