<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.8.2-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For the modelling of spatial non-stationarity at BS side, if physical blocker-based approach is adopted, the nearest K blockers from BS are selected.
For the modelling of spatial non-stationarity at BS side, if physical blocker-based approach is adopted, at least for blockage model B, the following parameters to define the building edge are introduced in the Table 7.6.4.2-5 in TR 38.901:
Typical set of blockersBlocker dimensionsMobility patternOutdoorBuilding edge Cartesian: w=50 m; h=20 mStationary 
In the blockage model B, the following equation is used to calculate the attenuation caused by the building edge:
LdB=-20log100.5-F, where F represents one of Fh1, Fh2, Fw1 and Fw2 defined in equation 7.6-29 in section 7.6.4.2 of TR 38.901.
Note: Corresponding Working Assumption made in RAN1#119 does not need to be confirmed.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.8.2-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For near-field channel, the following formula is adopted to model the phase parameters of non-direct path between TRP and UE as antenna element-wise channel parameter:
For the TRP side, the element-wise phase is calculated as:
expj2πd1,n-d1,n∙ rtx,n,m-dtx,sλ0
where d1,n is the generated distance of the cluster n. rtx,n,m is the spherical unit vector with azimuth departure angle and elevation departure angle for ray m of cluster n. dtx,s is the vector pointing from reference point to transmit antenna element s, wherein the reference point is the physical center of the antenna array/center at Tx side.
For the UE side, the element-wise phase is calculated as:
expj2πd2,n-d2,n∙ rrx,n,m-drx,uλ0
where d2,n is the generated distance of the cluster n. rrx,n,m is the spherical unit vector with azimuth arrival angle and elevation arrival angle for ray m of cluster n. drx,u is the vector pointing from reference point to receive antenna element u, wherein the reference point is the physical center of the antenna array/center at Rx side.


Final summary in R1-2501485.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120-9.9.1-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Confirm the following working assumption made in RAN1#118bis
Working Assumption(RAN1#118bis)
In addition to periodic CSI-RS, semi-persistent CSI-RS is supported for candidate cell L1-RSRP measurement for gNB scheduled reporting from RAN1 perspective
Send an LS to RAN3 (CC RAN2) to ask for the feasibility of specifying the signalling for coordination between serving cell and candidate cell(s) on the transmission of semi-persistent CSI-RS(s) and any other potential issues (e.g. RAN3 workload).
Support of semi-persistent CSI-RS is subject to UE capability.
MAC CE is used to activate/deactivate the semi-persistent CSI-RS resource similarly to the legacy mechanism for a serving cell which will be specified in RAN2
Send an LS to RAN2 to inform about this agreement.
R1-2501499[Draft] LS on activation/deactivation of semi-persistent CSI-RS resource for LTM candidate cellsModerator (Fujitsu)
Thursday decision: The draft LS is endorsed. Final LS is approved in R1-2501500.

""" .
