<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120b-9.8.2-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For the modelling of spatial non-stationarity, if the unified visible probability and visibility region based approach is adopted, for the Step 1 (whether a cluster is impacted by SNS) is determined as:
For the nth UE, the Prn is generated using a truncated normal distribution within [0,1]
Prn=Nμ, σ2;     where 0≤Prn≤1.
FFS: the value of μ, σ.
Note: It should be fixed in RAN1#120-bis;
For kth cluster of the nth user, if the xk,n is smaller than Prn, the cluster is impacted by the SNS, where the xk,n is defined as xk,n~U(0,1))
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120b-9.8.2-002> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For the modelling of spatial non-stationarity, if the unified visible probability and visibility region based approach is adopted, generate the visibility region as a rectangle randomly located at a corner of the antenna array with dimension a*b, where a~U(Vn*W,W), b=Vn*H*W/a, H is the antenna array height in vertical dimension and W is the antenna array width in horizontal dimension, Vn is calculated by
Vn=Α∙e-maxPn-Pnλ+Β+δ.
where A=0.15, B=0.45, λ=33, δ~N(0,0.0015) for UMa scenario, and n is a cluster index
FFS: The value for other scenarios.
Note: It should be fixed in RAN1#120-bis;
FFS: the details of randomly located VR
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120b-9.8.2-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For the modelling of spatial non-stationarity, if the unified visible probability and visibility region based approach is adopted,
For clusters without SNS, the power attenuation factor αs,n is set to 1.
For clusters with SNS, the power attenuation factor αs,n is generated by
αs,n=1                             ,xs-x0,n≤a,ys-y0,n≤be-xs-xa,nDn∙C        ,xs-x0,n>a,ys-y0,n≤b  e-ys-yb,nDn∙C        ,xs-x0,n≤a,ys-y0,n>b e-xs-xa,n2+ys-yb,n2Dn∙C                          ,others  
where, Dn=xA,n-xa,n2+yB,n-yb,n2 , xA,n, yB,n is the coordinate of the other corner of the antenna array on the diagonal with reference corner x0,n, y0,n, and xa,n, yb,n is the coordinate of the other corner of the rectangular VR on the diagonal with reference corner x0,n, y0,n. The xs, ys denotes the coordinate of the antenna element out of VR region. C is the roll-off factor between the visible and invisible regions. 
FFS: The value of C.
Note: It should be fixed in RAN1#120-bis;


R1-2503025Summary#2 of channel model adaptation and extensionModerator (ZTE)
From Wednesday session""" .
