<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120b-9.8.2-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For near-field channel, the scaling factor (sUE,n) used to generate the d2 is:
For number of k1 non-direct paths, sUE,n=1.
For number of k2 non-direct paths:
Option-1: sUE,n=1-sTRP,n;
Note 1: It’s assumed that only single non-specular interaction along with specular reflection(s) is considered in the propagation channel
Note 2: At least most of the sources of non-specular interaction are assumed to be a point scatterer or diffractions.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-120b-9.8.2-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For near-field channel, to generate the d1 for the k2 non-direct paths, the distribution of scaling factor sTRP,n is:
For the UMi scenarios, a Beta distribution with α=1.53, β=1.42
For the UMa scenarios, a Beta distribution with α=1.93, β=1.33
For the InH scenarios, a Beta distribution with α=1.25, β=1.27
""" .
