""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-121-9.7.2-036> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The existing blockage model A/B procedures can be reused to model the blocking effect due to a target as an optional feature 
Applicable to the LOS/NLOS rays in the background channel of the target
Applicable to the LOS/NLOS rays in the Tx-target and target-Rx link of another target
The location, orientation and size of the target as a blocker is known before applying the blockage model A/B.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-121-9.7.2-037> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The square brackets on formula 7.9.5-10 (copied below) in the draft CR are removed
The effective polarization matrix of the type-2 EO reflection path is given by
[CPMEO=cosγ2sinγ2-sinγ2cosγ2R∥00-R⊥cosγ1-sinγ1sinγ1cosγ1(7.9.5-10)]

Encourage companies to check and compare with the results that can be obtained with Alt2 and Alt3 below. If problem is found, RAN1 will revise TR 38.901 by new CR.
Alt2
[CPMEO=cosγ2-sinγ2sinγ2cosγ2R∥00-R⊥cosγ1sinγ1-sinγ1cosγ1(7.9.5-10)]
with reusing the legacy transformation method for deriving γ1 and γ2.

Alt3
[CPMEO=cosγ2-sinγ2sinγ2cosγ2R∥00-R⊥cosγ1sinγ1-sinγ1cosγ1(7.9.5-10)]
Where, 
γ1=atan2-eθEO, ZODnplane,eϕEO, AODnplane. nplane represents the normal vector of the incident plane. nplane=vtx→w×vw→rx, in which vtx→w=xw-xtx,yw-ytx,zw-ztx and vw→rx=xrx-xw,yrx-yw,zrx-zw. eθEO, ZOD represents the spherical basis vector of incident ray in vertical direction. eθEO,ZOD=cosθEO, ZODcosϕEO, AOD,cosθEO, ZODsinϕEO, AOD,-sinθEO, ZODT. eϕEO,AOD represents the spherical basis vector of incident ray in horizontal direction. eϕEO,AOD=-sinφEO, AOD,cosφEO, AOD,0T. 
γ2=atan2-eθEO, ZOAnplane,eϕEO, AOAnplane. eθEO, ZOA represents the polar basis vector of scattering ray in vertical direction. eϕEO, AOA represents the polar basis vector of scattering ray in horizontal direction. eθEO, ZOA=cosθEO, ZOAcosϕEO, AOA,cosθEO, ZOAsinϕEO, AOA,-sinθEO, ZOAT. eϕEO, AOA=-sinϕEO, AOA,cosϕEO, AOA,0T. 
""" .
