FFS: Whether/what new information is provided in SCell activation command?""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.2.2-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement: 
For early triggering of CSI/CSI-RS when SCell transition from deactivation to activation, support aperiodic CSI reporting for a SCell triggered based on legacy SCell activation command activating the SCell.
The aperiodic CSI reporting is assosicated with at least aperiodic CSI-RS for CSI on the SCell
FFS: Timeline of the aperiodic CSI reporting and corresponding aperiodic CSI-RS for CSI (requirement is up to RAN4) 
FFS: How to trigger the aperiodic CSI reporting and corresponding aperiodic CSI-RS for CSI based on legacy SCell activation command?
FFS: Whether/what new information is provided in SCell activation command?""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.2.2-008> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement: 
For early triggering of SRS-AS/CSI-RS/CSI when UE transition from IDLE to CONNECTED mode, study the following at least three options for Step-1 and Step-2:
Option-1: NW can provide the resource/report configuration in SIBx based on only one UE capability assumption, and UE can report through MSG3 whether the resource/report configuration received in SIBx is supported.
Option-2: NW can provide the resource/report configuration(s) in SIBx based on one or multiple UE capability assumptions, and UE can report through MSG3 which resource/report configuration(s) received in SIBx is/are supported.
Option-3: NW can provide the resource/report configuration(s) in SIBx based on one or multiple UE capability assumptions, and UE can report through MSG3 the supported capability(s) of early SRS/CSI/CSI-RS triggering (e.g., whether to support this feature, max number of CSI-RS ports, xTyR for SRS-AS, max bandwidth of the CSI-RS/SRS-AS etc.).
Note: The term “capability” or “UE capability” above does not mean legacy RRC based UE capability.

""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, Budget-Alt2 (as per TR38.769) is used to derive Rx sensitivity in the evaluation for both R2D and D2R.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-002> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, channel model TDL-C with an RMS delay spread of 300 ns delay spread is used for link level simulation for NLOS.


R1-2506459FL summary #2 for Ambient IoT: “10.3.1 Evaluations”Moderator (Huawei)
From Tuesday session""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, the followings is used to perform coverage evaluation for R2D and D2R, as for Rel-19:
Step 1: Obtain the required SINR by link-level simulations under different reference data rates
Step 2: Obtain the receiver sensitivity based on the required SINR if Budget-Alt2 is used
Step 3: Obtain the MPL/distance based on the receiver sensitivity and link budget calculation""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-004> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, the following path-loss models are used in the coverage evaluation:
UMa NLOS defined in TR38.901
RMa NLOS defined in TR38.901
Note: companies can also report to use RMa LOS defined in TR38.901
UMi NLOS defined in TR38.901
Note: this does not have implication on the coverage target (if any)""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-005> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, the antenna height for BS and Device used for evaluation purpose are as follows:
BS antenna height
UMa: 25m
RMa: 35m
UMi: 10m
Device antenna height
1.5m""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, the following layout assumption is used for evaluation purpose:
Hexagonal grid, 19 macro sites, 3 sectors per site
Note: the same layout assumption is used for UMi.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, BS Tx power assumption for coverage purpose is from the following:
For standalone: 43 dBm
For in-band:
38 or 33 dBm over R2D transmission BW
Note1: any necessary PSD limitation can be applied by RAN4.
Note2: companies should report any PSD limitation they assume in their RAN1 evaluations.
Send an LS to RAN4 with the above agreement, and to provide feedback to RAN1 if any.
Comeback for draft LS, considering potential further agreement on candidate R2D transmission BW.
R1-2506574Draft LS on BS Tx power assumption for coverage evaluation in A-IoTModerator (Huawei)
Thursday decision: The draft LS to RAN4 in R1-2506574 is endorsed. Final LS is approved in R1-2506575.

""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-008> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, Device Tx power assumption for evaluation purpose is from the following:
Device 2b: {-10, -20} dBm
Device C: {-3, 0, 5} dBm""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-009> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, BS antenna gain assumption in link budget for evaluation purpose:
17dBi
This assumes in the LLS table (as per TR38.769), the values in “[0h1] Number of antenna elements” and “[0h2] the Number of TXRUs” would be same (as Rel-19).""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-010> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, Device antenna gain assumption in link budget for evaluation purpose is 0dBi for both Device 2b and C.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-011> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, BS noise figure assumption in link budget for evaluation purpose is 5dB.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-012> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, R2D transmission bandwidth assumption in link budget and LLS for evaluation purpose is from the followings:
180kHz as starting point
Other values e.g. 360kHz, 540kHz or other multiples of 180kHz are not precluded and up to company report.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-013> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, R2D receiver bandwidth assumption in link budget and LLS for evaluation purpose is up to company report with considering:
R2D transmission bandwidth
Device Rx LO uncertainty (e.g. CFO ppm assumption)
Note: ED bandwidth (for the purpose of noise/interference power calculation, if any) and BB LPF bandwidth in LLS are assumed to be same as R2D receiver bandwidth in link budget for active device with ZIF/IF receiver.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-014> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, D2R transmission bandwidth assumption in link budget and LLS for evaluation purpose is from the followings:
15kHz as starting point
Other values are not precluded and up to company report.
Companies to report which of 2SB or 1SB modulation is assumed for D2R transmission bandwidth.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.1-015> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For Rel-20 study, message size in LLS assumption for evaluation purpose is from the following:
