<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Study necessity and feasibility of reuse, modifications or enhancements of existing Rel-19 D2R modulations, and the potential introduction of new modulations schemes, for Device 2b and for Device C, including at least the following aspects:
introduction of new modulation schemes (e.g., MSK or DBPSK)
down-selection of existing modulation schemes
design considerations related to spectrum shaping and D2R signals""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Study the following aspects to support DO-A traffic (periodic and event-triggered) for Device 2b and for Device C in Rel-20.
Timing and frequency synchronization for DO-A transmission
Resource allocation/determination method for DO-A transmission
Configuration/signaling of necessary information""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-008> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Study necessity and feasibility of enhancements on existing Rel-19 D2R FEC for Device 2b and for Device C including the following aspects:
additional FEC code rate(s) (e.g., 1/2, 1/4)
interleaver, or LTE bit collection scheme for TBCC
Note: no change to Rel-19 TBCC polynomial.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-009> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For PDRCH, study necessity and feasibility of larger (>2) number of repetitions for block-level repetitions for Device 2b and for Device C.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-010> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For PDRCH, study necessity of scrambling for Device 2b and for Device C.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-011> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
At least for CBRA for DT and DO-DTT, study necessity and feasibility of enhancements of D2R TDM(A) for Device 2b and for Device C based on the following:
X1 > 2 for Msg1 (X1: number of time domain resources for Msg1 transmission indicated by the corresponding R2D message)
X3 > 1 for Msg3 (X3: number of time domain resources for Msg3 transmission indicated by the corresponding R2D message)""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-012> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Study necessity and feasibility of enhancements of D2R for Device 2b and for Device C, considering the following aspects or potential enhancements:
Considering that Device 2b and Device C can adjust the LO towards a desired frequency, whether to also support baseband small FS for Device 2b and Device C
D2R frequency resources for FDM(A) (e.g., considering D2R transmission bandwidth, guard-band size between FDMed D2R transmissions, CFO, SFO, etc.)
How a device determines the frequency resource for D2R transmission
FDM(A) for D2R transmissions other than Msg1 and Msg3""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-013> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Study necessity and feasibility of D2R Tx power control for Device 2b and for Device C, including the following aspects
Open loop and/or closed loop power control
Required measurements (e.g., signal strength)
Required information at the device
Required information at reader side
Signaling overhead and power consumption

R1-2506593FL summary #6 for 10.3.2 “Study of air interface for Device 2b/C”Moderator (LG Electronics)
From Friday session""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.3.2-014> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
At least for DT and DO-DTT, study necessity and feasibility of changes to existing timing offsets for Device 2b and for Device C, e.g., 
timing offset value between R2D and corresponding subsequent D2R (e.g., Toffset1/2/3/4)
timing offset value between D2R and corresponding subsequent R2D (e.g., T_D2R_min)
Note: RAN1 only discusses potential reasons that may impact the value of T_D2R_min, and if any provides those reasons to RAN4
timing offset between R2D and corresponding subsequent D2R provided by a reader
timing offset between D2R and corresponding subsequent R2D provided by a reader.
At least for DT and DO-DTT, study necessity and feasibility of introduction of new timing offsets for Device 2b and for Device C, e.g.,
timing offset between two consecutive R2D or D2R transmissions for the same Device, if such scenario exists.


Final summary in R1-2506594.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-10.5.1-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Horizontal/vertical positioning accuracy are agreed as performance metrics for NR ISAC. 
It is defined as the absolute value of the difference between the estimated horizontal/vertical position and the corresponding true position of a sensing target. 
Note: in RAN1 evaluations, there should be only one estimated horizontal/vertical position corresponding to the true position of a sensing target.


