<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.13.1-005> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Adopt the following text proposal for TS 36.211, with a separate UE capability for the newly added alternative:
Reason for change: In some cases, it is observed that an alternative value of the cyclic shift may provide performance improvement;
Summary of changes: Add two new methods for cyclic shift;
Consequence if not approved: New values of cyclic shift are not supported.
******** start of TP *************
6.5.1Cyclic Shift for PMCH
The input to the cyclic shift is the block of bits b0, …, bMbit-1 defined in clause 6.3.1 and the ouput is a block of bits b0, …, bMbit-1.
The block of bits b0, …, bMbit-1 shall be cyclically shifted by Xi bits to form the block b0, …, bMbit-1 according to
bn=b(n-Xi mod Mbit)
where
-Xi is given by
Xi=r=C-SiC-1Er
Si=iα mod C
-i∈0, 1, …, N-1 denotes the ith subframe to which the transport block is mapped
-N is the number of subframes to which the transport block is mapped
-Er is the number of bits in the rth codeblock within a subframe as defined in TS 36.212 [3]
-C is the number of codeblocks in the transport block
-α is given by
-if the higher-layer parameter XXX is set to alphaOne
α=1
-if the higher-layer parameter XXX is set to alphaOther
α=CNL

if the higher-layer parameter XXX is set to alphaOther2
Xi= Ainf ,nSF×floor(NSC ×QmN), Ainf ,nSF ∈{0,…N-1}  
where Ainf ,nSF= m=07c8nf mod 12810+nSF+m2mmod N where nf is the system frame number and nSF is subframe number within the frame. The pseudo-random sequence ci is defined by clause 7.2 and shall be initialized with cinit=NIDMBSFN at the beginning of each radio frame for which nf mod 128=0, where  NSC  is the number of subcarriers available in 1 OFDM symbol for PMCH,  NSC =Mbit/(QmL), Qm is the modulation order.
where L is the number of OFDM symbols used for the PMCH transmission.
******** end of TP *************
""" .
