<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.7-013> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The TP below is endorsed for TR 38.901 v19.0.0.

<Start of Changes>7.9.5.5Lower power clustersIn addition to the clusters/rays in background channel generated in Clause 7.9.4.2, more clusters/rays using NLOS propagation condition can be generated between a sensing Tx and a sensing Rx for bi-static sensing or between a sensing Tx and a reference point r, where r=0, 1, 2 for mono-static sensing to simulate the weak rays in the background channel. The following procedure is applicable for bistatic sensing or for monostatic sensing. Step 1: Generate a first background channel Hu,sbk1τ,t for bi-static sensing and Hu,sbk1,rτ,t for referenc point r for mono-static sensing according to Clause 7.9.4.2. Step 2: Generate a second background channel Hu,sbk2τ,t for bi-static sensing and Hu,sbk2,rτ,t for reference point r for mono-static sensing according to Clause 7.9.4.2 including utilizing the same DS, ASA, ASD, ZSA, ZSD, Cθ, Cϕas used for the first step, if applicable, with the following revised parameters: 1) The number of clusters (N in Clause 7.5) is increased to 360; 2) The number of ray per cluster (M in Clause 7.5) is reduced to 1; 3) If LOS condition is assumed in Step 1, use NLOS condition to generate DS, ASA, ASD, ZSA, and ZSD values.  Step 3: The power of the clusters/rays in the second background channel is scaled down by PmaxS110G10, and is added to the first background channel, where, G=-25 dB, PmaxS1 is the maximum power of the NLOS clusters in the first background channel for bi-static sensing and PmaxS1,r is the maximum power of the NLOS clusters for reference point r in the first background channel. The final background channel Hu,sbkτ,t is 7.9.5-15a for bi-static sensing mode and 7.9.5-15b for mono-static sensing.Hu,sbkτ,t=Hu,sbk1τ,t+PmaxS1 10G10 P1S110G10∙Hu,sbk2τ,t(7.9.5-15a)Hu,sbkτ,t=Hu,sbk1τ,t+r=02PmaxS1,r 10G10∙Hu,sbk2,rτ,t  (7.9.5-15b)<End of Changes>
""" .
