The following TP is endorsed for TR 38.901 v19.0.0.
7.9.4.2.Background channel<omitted text>Step 2: Generate 3 reference points (RPs) for the STX/SRX.Draw the 2D distance between the STX/SRX and each RP and the height of each RP respectively by ΓGαd,βd+cd and ΓGαh,βh+ch with parameters defined in Table 7.9.4.2-1/2. Note that Gαd,βd and Gαh,βh are random values generated by the shape-rate parameterized Gamma distribution fx|α,β=βαΓ(α)xα-1e-βx. With uniform distribution within range -π,π, draw the LOS AOD (ϕLOS,AOD) between the STX/SRX and the first RP. The LOS AOD is further rotated by 23π and 43π to respectively derive the LOS AOD from the STX/SRX to the second and third RPs. Consequently, the 3D location of each RP can be calculated. <omitted text>
""" .
