In case of polarized antenna elements assume ζ is the polarization slant angle where ζ=0  degrees corresponds to a purely vertically polarized antenna element and ζ=±45 degrees correspond to a pair of cross-polarized antenna elements. Then the antenna element field components in θ' and ϕ' direction are given by
Fθ''θ',ϕ'Fϕ''θ',ϕ'=+cosψ-sinψ+sinψ+cosψFθ''''θ'',ϕ''Fϕ''''θ'',ϕ'',                                        (7.3-3)
where 
cosψ=cosζsinθ'+sinζsinϕ'cosθ'1-cosζsincosθ'-sinζsinϕ'cossinθ'2,                                                (7.3-3a)
sinψ=sinζcosϕ'1-cosζcosθ'-sinζsinϕ'sinθ'2.                                                     (7.3-3b)
