<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.8-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Adopt the following TP to TR38.901
Reason for change: Breaking up the cluster and ray scaling angles for CDL angle scaling, such that other WG may be able to reference the TR easily. Also improves readability of the angle scaling for CDL models.
Summary of change: introduce an intermediate variable to represent cluster angles, which are the angles being scaled by the model.
Consequences if not approved: Difficult for WGs to identify scaled angle component in CDL models.
===== Start of TP for TR38.901=====
7.7.5.1CDL extension: Scaling of angles
The angle values of CDL models are fixed, which is not very suitable for MIMO simulations for several reasons; The PMI statistics can become biased, and a fixed precoder may perform better than open-loop and on par with closed-loop or reciprocity beamforming. Furthermore, a CDL only represents a single channel realization. The predefined angle values in the CDL models can be generalized by introducing angular translation and scaling. By translation, mean angle μϕ,model can be changed to μϕ,desired  and angular spread ASmodel can be changed to match ASdesired by scaling. The translated and scaled ray angles can be obtained according to the following equation:
ϕn,m,scaled=ϕn,scaledϕn,intermediate-μϕ,intermediate+μϕ,desired+c{ASA, ASD,ZSA,ZSD}αm(7.7-5)
ϕLOS,scaled=ϕLOS,intermediate-μϕ,intermediate+μϕ,desired(7.7-5a)
ϕn,intermediate=s∙WrapTo180ϕn,model-μϕ,model(7.7-5b)
ϕLOS,intermediate=s∙WrapTo180ϕLOS,model-μϕ,model(7.7-5c)
ϕn,scaled=ϕn,intermediate-μϕ,intermediate+μϕ,desired(7.7-5d)
in which:
< Unchanged text omitted >
-ASdesiredis the desired rms cluster angular spread,
-ϕn,scaledis the scaled CDL cluster angle of the nth cluster,
-ϕn,m,scaled is the resulting scaled ray angle that corresponds to mth subpath angle of nth cluster,
< Unchanged text omitted >
Alternatively, for CDL-D and CDL-E, if maintaining the LOS angle is desired, the translated and scaled ray angles can be obtained according to the following equation instead of using equation (7.7-5) and (7.7-5a):
ϕn,m,scaled=ϕn,scaledϕn,intermediate-ϕLOS,intermediate+ϕLOS,model+c{ASA, ASD,ZSA,ZSD}αm(7.7-6)
ϕLOS,scaled=ϕLOS,model(7.7-6a)
ϕn,scaled=ϕn,intermediate-ϕLOS,intermediate+ϕLOS,model(7.7-6b)
in which:
-ϕLOS,model is the LOS path angle of the model.
-ϕn,scaled is the scaled CDL cluster angle of the nth cluster,
< Unchanged text omitted >
===== End of TP for TR38.901=====

Agreement (modified in Friday session)
Adopt the following TP to TR38.901
Reason for change: Ambiguous application of antenna polarization for the handheld UT antenna.
Summary of change: Clarify the polarization equation for handheld UT
Consequences if not approved: Polarization application for handheld UT is ambiguous and can lead to companies with different implementation.
===== Start of TP for TR38.901=====
7.3.2Polarized antenna modelling
Handheld UT Model:
< Unchanged parts are omitted >
Each polarized field component of the reference radiation pattern Fθ″″θ″,ϕ″ and Fϕ″″θ″,ϕ″ should be rotated according to the orientation and polarization direction of the each of UT antennae to get Fu,θ''θ',ϕ', Fu, ϕ''θ',ϕ' using equation (7.3-3), 
Fu,θ''θ',ϕ'Fu, ϕ''θ',ϕ'=+cosψu-sinψu+sinψu+cosψuFθ''''θ'',ϕ''Fϕ''''θ'',ϕ'',                                 (7.3-6)
cosψu=cosβucosγusinθ'-sinβucosγucosϕ'-αu-sinγusinϕ'-αucosθ'1-cosβucosγucosθ'+sinβucosγucosϕ'-αu-sinγusinϕ'-αusinθ'2                    (7.3-7)
sinψu=sinβucosγusinϕ'-αu+sinγucosϕ'-αu1-cosβucosγucosθ'+sinβucosγucosϕ'-αu-sinγusinϕ'-αusinθ'2                    (7.3-8)
where the 3D-rotation angles, αu, βu and γu, are obtained according to the orientation and polarization direction of each UT antenna u, and then rotated based on the orientation of the UT in the global coordinate system to get Fu,θθ,ϕ and Fu,ϕθ,ϕ using Clause 7.1.3 equation (7.1-11).
< Unchanged parts are omitted >
===== End of TP for TR38.901=====
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.8-004> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Adopt the following TP to TR38.901
Reason for change: In the current TR 38.901 [1], antenna element-wise angular-domain parameters are introduced to additionally model the antenna element-wise field patterns for the NLOS channel impulse response in the near-field channel model. However, the definitions of these antenna element-wise angular-domain parameters are missing, leading to ambiguity in their interpretation.
Summary of change: Add definitions for the antenna element-wise angular-domain parameters in equation 7.6-49 of TR 38.901 [1], which are introduced for modelling the antenna element-wise field patterns.
Consequences if not approved: The expression for the angular-domain parameters in equation 7.6-49 of TR 38.901 [1] remains undefined, resulting in ambiguity and potential inconsistency in implementation.
===== Start of TP for TR38.901=====
7.6.13Near-field channel model
<Unrelated parts are omitted>
-To model the antenna element-wise antenna field patterns additionally, the Hu,s,n,mNLOSt is given by:
Hu,s,n,mNLOSt=PnMFrx,u,θθn,m,ZOA,u,ϕn,m,AOA,uFrx,u,ϕθn,m,ZOA,u,ϕn,m,AOA,uTexpjΦn,mθθkn,m-1expjΦn,mθϕkn,m-1expjΦn,mϕθexpjΦn,mϕϕFtx,s,θθn,m,ZOD,s,ϕn,m,AOD,sFtx,s,ϕθn,m,ZOD,s,ϕn,m,AOD,s
expj2πd2,n,m-d2,n,m∙ rrx,n,m-drx,uλ0expj2πd1,n,m-d1,n,m∙ rtx,n,m-dtx,sλ0expj2πrrx,n,mT∙vλ0t(7.6-49)
where θn,m,ZOA,u and ϕn,m,AOA,u are the antenna element-wise elevation arrival angles and azimuth arrival angles, respectively, for ray m of cluster n for receive antenna element u, and θn,m,ZOD,s and ϕn,m,AOD,s are the antenna element-wise elevation departure angles and azimuth departure angles, respectively, for ray m of cluster n for transmit antenna element s.
