<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.8-005> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Adopt the following TP to TR38.901
Reason for change: variable K is being used for Rician factor and number of blockers in the TR. However, Clause 3.3. definition for K clearly describes K being Rician factor. Causing potential confusion.
Summary of chang: Update variable K used for number of blockers in Clause 7.6.4 to Kblock.
Consequences if not approved: Ambiguous usage of K variable for two different functionality.
===== Start of TP for TR38.901=====
7.6.4.1Blockage model A
Model A adopts a stochastic method for capturing human and vehicular blocking. 
Step a: Determine the number of blockers.
Multiple 2-dimensional (2D) angular blocking regions, in terms of centre angle, azimuth and elevation angular span are generated around the UT. There is one self-blocking region, and K Kblock = 4 non-self-blocking regions, where K Kblock may be changed for certain scenarios (e.g., higher blocker density). Note that the self-blocking component of the model is important in capturing the effects of human body blocking. 
<unchanged text omitted>
7.6.4.2Blockage model B
Model B adopts a geometric method for capturing e.g., human and vehicular blocking. 
Step a: Determine blockers
A number, K Kblock, of blockers are modelled as rectangular screens that are physically placed on the map. Each screen has the dimension by height () and width (), with the screen centre at coordinate . 
Note: 
-The number of blockers (K Kblock), their vertical and horizontal extensions ( and ), locations , density, and movement pattern (if non-stationary) are all simulation assumptions, to allow different blocking scenarios to be constructed depending on the need of the particular simulation study.
Recommended parameters for typical blockers are provided in Table 7.6.4.2-5. 
-The blocking effect diminishes with increasing distance to the blocker. For implementation purposes it may be sufficient to consider only the K Kblock nearest blockers or the blockers closer than some distance from a specific UT. 
<unchanged text omitted>
===== End of TP for TR38.901=====
""" .
