Fu,θ''θ',ϕ'Fu, ϕ''θ',ϕ'=+cosψu-sinψu+sinψu+cosψuFθ''''θ'',ϕ''Fϕ''''θ'',ϕ'',                                 (7.3-6)
cosψu=cosβucosγusinθ'-sinβucosγucosϕ'-αu-sinγusinϕ'-αucosθ'1-cosβucosγucosθ'+sinβucosγucosϕ'-αu-sinγusinϕ'-αusinθ'2(7.3-7)
sinψu=sinβucosγusinϕ'-αu+sinγucosϕ'-αu1-cosβucosγucosθ'+sinβucosγucosϕ'-αu-sinγusinϕ'-αusinθ'2(7.3-8)
where the 3D-rotation angles, αu, βu and γu, are obtained according to the orientation and polarization direction of each UT antenna u, the zenith and azimuth angles mapping between θ',ϕ' and θ'',ϕ'' are based on equations (7.1-7) and (7.1-8) using the same 3D-rotation angles, αu, βu and γu, and then rotated based on the orientation of the UT in the global coordinate system to get Fu,θθ,ϕ and Fu,ϕθ,ϕ using Clause 7.1.3 equation (7.1-11).
< Unchanged parts are omitted >
===== End of TP for TR38.901=====
""" .
