<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.9.1-009> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For a UE capable of CSI acquisition of performing early CSI measurement operations before and after LTM Cell Switch Command MAC CE: 
For candidate cell(s), a periodic CSI-RS resource and port are counted as ‘active’ in a duration starting when the periodic CSI-RS resource is configured by higher layer signaling until the reception of the LTM cell switch command MAC CE or a RRC reconfiguration message, which comes first.
For candidate cell(s), a SP CSI-RS resource and port are counted as ‘active’ in a duration starting from the end of when the activation command is applied until the reception of the LTM cell switch command MAC CE or a deactivation command MAC CE, which comes first. 
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122-8.9.1-010> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For a UE capable of CSI acquisition of performing early CSI measurement operations only after LTM Cell Switch Command MAC CE: 
For candidate cell(s), periodic and SP-CSI-RS resources and ports configured for early CSI acquisition in an LTM Candidate cell are not counted as active before reception of LTM Cell Switch Command MAC CE.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122b-10.1.1.1-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement:
Support precoding matrix with port-subband domain representation as target CSI type.
For a certain layer l, a precoding matrix on N_sb subband and P CSI-RS ports is Winl=[Win,0l, Win,1l,⋯,Win, Nsb-1l] with Win,kl being a P×1 vector.
Note: Only sub-band PMI reporting is supported.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122b-10.1.1.1-002> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement:
For determining the payload parameters combinations dl,ν,Ql,ν or dl,ν,L,Ql,ν  across all layers and ranks, consider following general principles for precoding matrix-based target CSI
Rank-common and layer-common model with payload-scalable design is considered as the baseline implementation for discussion purpose. 
Note: layer-specific / rank-specific (if supported) payload parameters are supported by this rank-common and layer-common model with payload-scalable design.
Limiting the total number of (per-layer) payload parameters combinations dl,ν,Ql,ν or dl,ν,L,Ql,ν  across all layers and all ranks.
At least for medium to high per-layer payload regime, the total payload size of rank 2, rank 3 and 4 are comparable to each other.
Spectral efficiency or system throughput and trade-off with feedback overhead are considered as the performance metric.

""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122b-10.1.1.1-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement:
When the Target CSI is precoder matrix, in order to down-select to N per-layer payload parameter combinations (PC) of dl,ν,Ql,ν or dl,ν, L,Ql,ν based on performance, overhead and complexity trade-off results, consider the following candidate values:
Candiate values for dl,ν: 32, 64, 96, 128, 192
Candidate values for Ql,ν: 1, 2, 3, 4, (8, 10 only for VQ)
2 is considered as the baseline assumption for SQ.
Candidate values for L: L=2, 4,  dl,ν
Candidate values for N: 4, 5, 6
Note: These N payload PCs of dl,ν,Ql,ν or dl,ν, L,Ql,ν are considered as the pool for the payload PC for each layer and each rank.
Note: The above is for discussion purpose, how to configure the PCs (across layers and ranks) is a separate discussion.
Note: Rank-common and layer-common model with payload scalable design is considered.
Note: The above does not mean support of both SQ and VQ.
Note: The number of parameters combinations configurations (Y) does not exceed 8.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122b-10.1.1.1-004> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement:
For payload parameter combinations (PC), consider followings 
Support Y configurable PCs (across layers and ranks) as below, where X_n, Xn_31, Xn_32, Xn_33, Xn_41, Xn_42, Xn_43, Xn_44 represent a pair of dl,ν,Ql,ν or a triplet of dl,ν, L,Ql,ν  chosen from the per-layer PC pool. 
Rank1Rank2Rank3Rank4PC1X1X1, X1X1_31, X1_32, X1_33X1_41, X1_42, X1_43, X1_44PC2X2X2, X2X2_31, X2_32, X2_33X2_41, X2_42, X2_43, X2_44…

For rank 1 and rank 2, layer-common and rank-common payload is supported.
For rank 3, consider alternatives of {Xn_31, Xn_32, Xn_33} = {a, a, a}, {a, a, b}, {a, b, b} for potential down selection.
For rank 4, consider alternatives of {Xn_41, Xn_42, Xn_43, Xn_44} = {a, a, a, a}, {a, a, b, b}, {a, b, b, c}, {a, a, b, c} or {a, b, c, c} for potential down selection.
Note: The table is for discussion purpose, how to configure the PCs (across layers and ranks) is a separate discussion.
Note: a, b values in rank3 can be different from that in rank 4.
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-122b-10.1.1.1-005> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement:
