R1-2508743FL summary #2 for Ambient IoT: “10.3.1 Evaluations”Moderator (Huawei)""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.1-003> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The following energy harvesting/storage assumptions used to obtain the reported data rates from companies are provided during the Rel-20 study
Note: Companies can further add their reports until RAN1#124
SourceEnergy harvesting/storage assumptionsSource [Huawei]Energy source:Solar power/lightEnergy storage capacity:~300 mF capacitor for low data rates~60 mF capacitor for middle data rates~40 mF capacitor for high data rates High voltage 2.7 V, low voltage 1.1 VReported data rate:Low data rate: ~ 0.1 kbps for D2R and ~ 1 kbps for R2DMiddle data rate: ~ 1 kbps for D2R and ~ 1 kbps for R2DHigh data rate: ~ 5 kbps for D2R and ~ 5 kbps for R2DOther information (if any):For D2R transmission, the consumed energy per hour isFor 0.1 kbps data rate: ~50 mJFor 1 kbps data rate: ~6.25 mJFor 5-7 kbps data rate: ~1.6 mJFor R2D transmission, the consumed energy per hour isFor 1 kbps data rate: 4 mJFor 5-7 kbps data rate: 0.8 mJSource [vivo]Energy source:Energy sources with high energy conversion efficiency, e.g., solar, vibration, thermal, etc., can be considered.Energy storage capacity:>=1mJ for 1mW peak power consumption and >=10mJ for 10mW peak power consumption.Reported data rate:For D2R, data rate is 1kbps.Other information (if any):When considering energy storage capacity, device at least can finish one D2R transmission. For 1000bits and 1kbps data rate, the D2R transmission time is 1000ms. For device C, the peak power consumption is ≤ 1 mW to ≤ 10 mW as agreed. Thus, for 10mW peak power consumption the energy is at least larger than 10mW*1000ms, i.e., 10mJ. Assuming the rated maximum voltage is 3V and the minimum available voltage is 2V, it can be derived that the capacitance of capacitor should be larger than 4mF. And for 1mW peak power consumption. The energy is at least larger than 1mW*1000ms, i.e., 1mJ corresponding to 400uF capacitance of capacitor.Source [ZTE]Energy source:Solar or other energy source are used.RF energy harvesting is deprioritized Energy storage capacity:> 15 mJ for device 2b> 75 mJ for device CReported data rate:~ 4 kbps for R2D transmission~ 0.1 kbps for D2R transmissionOther information (if any):The energy storage of > 15 mJ (device 2c) and > 75 mJ (device C) is considered to support an entire CBRA process for multiple devices.For a single PDRCH transmission, assuming a D2R data rate of 0.1 kbps and a TBS of 400 bits, the transmission takes approximately 4 seconds. This requires Device 2b (with a Tx power consumption of 800 uW) to have an energy storage capacity greater than 3.2 mJ and Device C (with a Tx power consumption of 2 mW) greater than 8 mJ to support a single D2R transmission.Source [Tejas]Energy source:Solar/light energy harvesting Energy storage capacity:180-300 mF for Device 2b with voltage = 3.3 V. 180-1700 mF for Device C with voltage  = 5VReported data rate:R2D data rate is 12-15 kbps with M=2D2R data rate is 5-7 kbpsOther information (if any):energy conversion efficiency of energy harvester is considered as 80-90%. Device 2b power consumption is considered as 480 µW to 770 µW. Device 2b power consumption is considered as 1 mW to 10 mW.  Solar panel size for device 2b is 20x20 mm2 and Device C is 30x25 mm2. Source [NEC]Energy source: Solar energyEnergy storage capacity: 10~100µF with voltage of 3VReported data rate: 1 kbps or 5 – 7 kbpsOther information (if any): Device 2b and Device C harvest energy at similar rate.Source [QC]For device 2bEnergy source: RF signal/SolarEnergy storage capacity: 10s ~ 100s uF < 1mFReported data rate: 1.7/2.5/5kbpsOther information (if any):Device 2b, message size= 96 bits, tx duration = 2.28ms, device power consumption = 500uW, voltage = 1V, assumed only 50% of energy can be used.For device CEnergy source: SolarEnergy storage capacity:  1m ~ 10mFReported data rate: 1.7/2.5/5kbpsOther information (if any): Device C, message size= 96 bits, tx duration = 2.28ms, device power consumption = 5mW, voltage = 1V, assumed only 50% of energy can be used.FL notes: In addition, companies can also report any related information they would like to indicate e.g. message size, reception/transmission duration, device power consumption, voltage, etc. Companies can also report how they derive the reported energy storage capacity.Source [DCM]Energy source: Solar, thermal, etc.Energy storage capacity:For device 2b with 500uW peak power consumption:0.1kbps: ~5mJ/~20mF1kbps: ~500uJ/~2mF7kbps: ~71.4uJ~285uFFor device C with 10mW peak power consumption:0.1kbps: ~100mJ/~400mF1kbps: ~10mJ/~40mF7kbps: ~1.4mJ/~5.7mFReported data rate:0.1 kbps, 1kbps, 7kbpsOther information (if any):For the maximum message size, 1000 bits is assumed for single PRDCH/PDRCH transmission.For voltage, max voltage as 2V and min voltage as 1V are assumed.For power consumption of each device type, 500uW is assumed for device 2b and 10mW is assumed for device C.It should be noted that the reported capacity is for single PRDCH/PDRCH transmission. To sustain whole procedure of DT, DO-DTT, DO-A, larger capacity is required.Source [FUTUREWEI]Energy sources: solar, thermal, vibration etc.Energy storage capacity:For device 2b with 500uW peak power consumption:  0.5 milli-joules or 500 μF using 2V power supplyFor device C with 10mW peak power consumption:  10 milli-joules or 10000 μF using 2V power supplyReported data rate:1kbpsOther information (if any):It is observed that using RF energy harvesting is challenging as the energy source for Device 2b based on the following description.Typical leakage current for 500 μF capacitors is at least higher than 3 μA. With a supply voltage of 2 volts, the leakage current translates to ~ -22.2 dBm leakage power. Using RF harvesting is challenging in this case.Source [Samsung]Energy source: SolarEnergy storage capacity: 5μJ for device 2b, 30μJ for device CReported data rate: 5.3 kbps for DL 20 bits, 6.7 kbps for UL 20 bits, 7.2 kbps for DL 96 bits, 8.4 kbps for UL 96 bits; with an average of 40% charging time


