<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.2-019> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Further study following modulation schemes.
BPSK: The input bit “1” is mapped to the real-valued modulation symbol “1” and input bit “0” is mapped to the real-valued modulation symbol “-1” in the baseband.
OOK: The input bit “1” is mapped to the real-valued modulation symbol “1” and input bit “0” is mapped to the real-valued modulation symbol “0” in the baseband.
DBPSK: The n-th input bit bn is differentially encoded as dn=bn⊕dn-1, where dn and dn-1 are the n-th and n-1-th differentially encoded input bit and ⊕ is XOR operation. Then, the differentially encoded bits dn are modulated by BPSK.
MSK: The input bit “1” is mapped to frequency f1 and input bit “0” is mapped to frequency f2, with f2-f1=12T, where T is a symbol duration.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
