<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-004> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
The functionality of broadcast information is to provide the device with at least necessary information for subsequent transmission and reception
On how A-IoT devices acquire the broadcast information, study the following two cases: 
Case B1: Single-step acquisition of the broadcast information 
Case B2: Two-step acquisition of the broadcast information (e.g., MIB-like and then SIB1-like broadcast information)
On whether to use PRDCH to carry the broadcast information,
For Case B1, PRDCH is used to carry the broadcast information.
For Case B2 
PRDCH is used to carry the SIB1-like broadcast information.
A separate PRDCH or a new physical channel dedicated to MIB-like is used to carry the MIB-like broadcast information
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-005> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
Periodic transmission of broadcast information to provide at least necessary information for subsequent transmission and reception is necessary for Device 2b and for Device C.
FFS (in SI or WI): whether the transmission of broadcast information is strictly periodic at reader
FFS (in SI or WI): periodicity of the transmission of broadcast information""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For the 3 options for the content of the first D2R transmission for DO-A for Device 2b and for Device C, study the following aspects:
Recommended scenarios (event-triggered or periodic)
Subsequent transmission(s)/reception(s)/procedure(s) if any after the first D2R transmission for DO-A
Other aspects

R1-2509587FL summary #6 for 10.3.2.3 “Other procedures for Device 2b/C”Moderator (LG Electronics)
""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-007> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
On D2R Tx power control for Device 2b and for Device C, capture the following in TR 38.769.
The necessity of D2R Tx power control for Device 2b and Device C for outdoor scenarios were studied and the following observations were provided:
22 sources (Futurewei, LGE, Spreadtrum, vivo, Nokia, Semtech, CMCC, CEWiT, BOSCH, NEC, InterDigital, TCL, Apple, China Telecom, ZTE, OPPO, Huawei, Docomo, Ericsson, Xiaomi, Samsung, Qualcomm) reported that the D2R Tx power control for Device 2b and Device C is necessary for outdoor scenarios.
20 sources (Futurewei, LGE, Spreadtrum, vivo, Nokia, Semtech, CMCC, CEWiT, BOSCH, Quectel, InterDigital, TCL, Apple, OPPO, Huawei, Docomo, Ericsson, Xiaomi, Samsung, ZTE) state that it can reduce the interference between different devices (i.e., the Near-Far problem).
14 sources (Futurewei, LGE, Spreadtrum, vivo, Semtech, CMCC, NEC, InterDigital, TCL, Apple, OPPO, Xiaomi, Samsung, ZTE) reported that it helps devices remain available longer.
4 sources (Futurewei, Semtech, Apple, Docomo) reported that the interference due to a transmission from a device to a reader can be reduced at an unintended reader
1 source (Qualcomm) added that depending on device’s peak power consumption and PA support, the D2R Tx power control may not be feasible.
1 source (CATT) reported that the D2R Tx power control for Device 2b and Device C is not necessary mentioning in its contribution that the inter-channel interference from different devices is negligible, D2R coverage is limited, and the complexity and the power consumption required at the device side is high.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-008> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For reader identification/differentiation at least in outdoor scenario to differentiate R2D among different readers, a device acquires the reader ID-related information by at least one of the following options:
Option 1: Reader ID-related information is contained in the broadcast information.
Option 2: Reader ID-related information is derived from the periodic sync signal sequence(s).
Option 3: Reader ID-related information is carried by L1 R2D control information.
Option 4: Reader ID-related information is contained in the higher-layer information in the paging-like message.""" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-10.3.2.3-009> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For providing necessary information for the first D2R transmission for DO-A for Device 2b and for Device C, following options are considered feasible. 
Option 1: necessary information provided by broadcast information
Option 2: necessary information provided by a paging-like R2D message
Option 3: necessary information derived from a synchronization signal and provided by broadcast information
For providing necessary information for the first D2R transmission for DO-A for Device 2b and for Device C, study following option considering feasibility and applicability
Option 4: necessary information provided by device-specific R2D transmission""" .
