<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-11.5-006> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement
For the UE power model, assume: 
ΓB: The ratio of active bandwidth to the bandwidth of reference configuration (100 MHz)
ΓTput: The ratio of the maximum schedulable PDSCH throughput w.r.t. that of current active bandwidth, ΓTput∈{1, 1/2, 1/4}
FFS: How the maximum schedulable PDSCH throughput ratio ΓTput is ensured by NW
Companies to report the assumed technique to achieve the reduction in the maximum schedulable PDSCH throughput. Current techniques include at least: reduced scheduled maximum bandwidth, reduced scheduled maximum rank, and reduced scheduled duty cycle.
No antenna adaptation is assumed simultaneously
For evaluation purpose, 
Company to report Tmin value for the evaluation
T>Tmin is another relaxed adaptation delay. Company to report T value for the evaluation.
The adaptation delay is applied when adapting ΓB and/or ΓTput
Companies to report SMaxBW from one of the two options:
Option 1: SMaxBW=0 / Z1 / Z2 for Maximum BW (MaxBW) assumed for the evaluation ∈{100 MHz,200 MHz, 400 MHz}
Option 2: SMaxBW=0
Note: No implication on which configuration(s) and what adaptation(s) to be supported by 6GR

Include the following scaling for DL bandwidth adaptation for 6GR UE power consumption model:
For PDCCH+PDSCH:
ΓBΓTputScaling factor when adaptation delay T is assumedScaling factor when adaptation delay Tmin is assumed5%1X01X11 +SMaxBW20%1X02X12 +SMaxBW100%{1, 1/2}11+SMaxBW200%{1, 1/2}{X03, Y03}{X13, Y13} + SMaxBW400%{1, 1/2, 1/4}{X04, Y04, Z04}
For PDCCH-only: 
ΓBΓTputScaling factor when adaptation delay T is assumedScaling factor when adaptation delay Tmin is assumed5%1X21X31 +SMaxBW20%1X22X32 +SMaxBW100%111+SMaxBW200%{1, 1/2}{X23, Y23}{X33, Y33} + SMaxBW400%{1, 1/2, 1/4}{X24, Y24, Z24}
Other DL signal/channel processing:
ΓBScaling factor when adaptation delay T is assumedScaling factor when adaptation delay Tmin is assumed5%X41X51 +SMaxBW20%X42X52 +SMaxBW100%11+SMaxBW200%X43X53 + SMaxBW400%X44
Not applicable to sleep states and EE processing state
Further consolidate the table for cases of a same scaling factor
FFS: Scaling factor for other value(s) of ΓB<100%

For UL bandwidth adaptation,
No scaling for FR1 and around 7GHz
In case scaling is needed for FR2 (including 24.25 GHz – 52.6 GHz), companies can report the assumed scaling factor
Note: The term “bandwidth” used here is reusing the definition as 5GNR, which will be updated according to 6GR discussion
Note: All columns and rows of the above tables will be further checked, and corresponding values will be checked and confirmed/extended.


