<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN1/Resolution/AGR-123-6-001> spectra:sourceRecordWindowText """Agreement:
The following TP for TS36.211 for Rel-19 is endorsed.
Reason for change: Align RAN1 specifications to the field description of interferenceRandomisationConfig in TS 36.331 in Rel-19 IoT_NTN_Ph3.
Summary of Change: Add bullet “for NPDCCH associated with C-RNTI during random access procedure in a Type-2 CSS in an NB-IoT carrier configured by SystemInformationBlockType22-NB when interferenceRandomisationConfig is used, or” in Rel-19 IoT_NTN_Ph3. 
Consequences if not approved: RAN1 specification is not aligned to the field description of interferenceRandomisationConfig in TS 36.331.
Other comments: Implementation of this CR aligns RAN1 procedures (TS 36.211 clause 10.2.5.5) with the field description of interferenceRandomisationConfig in TS 36.331 and therefore will not cause compatibility issues with Rel-14 implementations until the present release.
10.2.5.5Mapping to resource elements------------------------------------------------------------ Text Omitted ------------------------------------------------------------------------------For frame structure type 1, -for NPDCCH associated with RA-RNTI, TC-RNTI, or for P-RNTI and transmitted in an NB-IoT carrier configured by SystemInformationBlockType22-NB, or -for NPDCCH associated with C-RNTI during random access procedure in a Type-2 CSS in an NB-IoT carrier configured by SystemInformationBlockType22-NB, or -for NPDCCH associated with C-RNTI in an NB-IoT carrier configured by SystemInformationBlockType22-NB when RadioResourceConfigDedicted-NB is not configured by higher layer, or -for NPDCCH associated with PUR-RNTI/G-RNTI/ SC-RNTI, or -for NPDCCH associated with C-RNTI or SPS C-RNTI when interferenceRandomisationConfig is used according to [9], or -------------------------------------------------------------- Text End ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The agreement above is captured in:
R1-2509559CR for Interference Randomization for non-anchor carrier in NB-IoT NTNMediaTek,  Ericsson, Qualcomm, Nordic Semiconductor ASA, Nokia, Nokia Shanghai Bell
(Rel-19, 36.211, NB_IOTenh-Core, TEI19, CR0581, Cat F) is agreed.


